# Per-machine secrets and API tokens — never commit. See AGENTS.md → Secrets.
.env

# Per-machine setup record — tooling, local auth, and specs that don't
# transfer across machines, so each one keeps its own copy. See
# AGENTS.md → Tracking machines and local setup.
local-setup.md

# devices.md is intentionally NOT ignored — the machine roster is tracked
# so every machine knows the others.

# Per-machine Claude Code overrides (model, local permissions, etc.).
.claude/settings.local.json

# Machine-local links into the top-level `skills/` folder (a directory junction
# on Windows, a symlink on Linux/macOS — Node's fs.symlinkSync picks per OS).
# Claude Code only discovers skills under `.claude/skills/`, and OpenAI Codex CLI
# discovers them under `.agents/skills/`; both are bridged to one source of
# truth. Recreated automatically by a SessionStart hook
# (.claude/hooks/ensure-skills-link.mjs) wired into both Claude Code
# (`.claude/settings.json`) and Codex (`.codex/hooks.json`).
# NOTE: no trailing slash — a Linux symlink is not a directory, so a
# `skills/` pattern would miss it and the link would get committed.
.claude/skills
.agents/skills

# App-owned, version-stamped content that Planet You writes into the AIOS. The
# app regenerates it per version, and spaces sync between machines and people
# who may be on different app versions, so tracking it would just churn.
# `.planetyou/` itself stays TRACKED so `settings.json` — your own preferences —
# syncs with the repo.
.planetyou/docs/
.planetyou/agents/

# Disposable, generated in-flight output: any `scratch/` folder, at any depth.
# The pattern carries no internal slash, so git applies it everywhere — most
# often `working/<task>/scratch/`. Gitignored means NOT synced and NOT backed
# up, so it's the right home for generated or throwaway output and the wrong
# home for thinking you'd be sad to lose.
scratch/

# Local vault: raw, private, un-triaged material (chat exports, dumps, Takeout
# archives, etc.). Staging area only — never committed. Promote distilled,
# non-sensitive pieces OUT into the tracked repo as they're cleaned up. The
# README stays tracked so the convention travels. (Born when first needed; the
# pack ships only this rule, not the folder.)
references/local-vault/*
!references/local-vault/README.md

# OS-generated cruft — never content, varies by machine/platform.
.DS_Store      # macOS Finder
Thumbs.db      # Windows Explorer thumbnails
Desktop.ini    # Windows folder settings
